    {
      "id": "claim_b78db1804aba4428b20eb3203d9cc46c",
      "statement": "Middleware is a non-runtime-checkable typing.Protocol with a single method __call__(dto) -> dto; anything callable with one positional argument (plain function, lambda, instance implementing __call__) is valid middleware, and there is no base class, no before/after hook and no async variant.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/middleware.md#L5-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:727f1d1bd25231631d3e2130dc439deb26e3e79bd1cdfa327b8c137cc67ed57a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://examples/middleware_examples.ipynb#L410-L432",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e3efae0f579fb1daa85f7dff05f8a267f66c4ee3ae22050d9662b72310378365:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/middleware.py#L4-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6632fe0408b910dc8b85f524f5ce953da0f41ccee21271768425341b8ff8049c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c1eda4f10fce4ed9ab2d3fd8b3d210db",
      "statement": "UseFramework.add_middleware only appends to MiddlewarePipeline.middlewares and performs no callable validation, so a non-callable entry fails at execution time inside the pipeline loop rather than at registration; MiddlewarePipeline.execute iterates the list forward and feeds each middleware the previous middleware's return value, making execution order identical to registration order with no priority, reordering, de-duplication or removal support.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/middleware.md#L58-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a47c2d925c8b43a0b4662b1da059b9dd5f6c755088bc8fa64c7196bbb8fe7c2:"
        },
