    {
      "id": "claim_16d98f08105642d7bff0c9b75456094e",
      "statement": "MiddlewarePipeline.execute captures dto.__class__ before the chain, runs the middleware chain, and if a middleware returned an object of a different class reassigns processed_dto.__class__ back to the captured class before calling executor(processed_dto, **kwargs); it has no try/except and no response phase, returning the executor's value directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/middleware.py#L34-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c01d35342a5c07b27b05bc1bcac1ca30a3d1d6316874819e207dc752474894a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52838c5a2e674626a7ef3f6ef1f94e25",
      "statement": "The __class__ restore is what keeps a middleware-transformed DTO routable: every bus derives its registry key from dto.__class__.__name__ at lookup time, so without the restore an enriched DTO type would raise UnknownDTOToExecute at the facade; only __class__ is reassigned, so the attributes added by the middleware travel with the instance while isinstance and __class__.__name__ again report the caller's original type.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L173-L194",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c85b7a2c97680bc4aa6ba7881fa36a602ed10a212893ee9e382cbf8ebd90944:"
        },
