    {
      "id": "claim_7b92a6cec1384cf6b9e7b206bc027a59",
      "statement": "Because the class restore happens before the executor runs, the registry lookup always uses the name of the class the caller passed, so a transforming middleware requires the handler to be registered against the caller's DTO type rather than the produced type.",
